.TH SCENE 5
.SH NAME
scene \- meshes and pictures to show
.SH DESCRIPTION
A scene file for
.IR view (1),
in the language of
.IR plicad (7),
has one item a line; file names are relative to the scene file.
.PP
.RS
.nf
mesh NAME FILE.obj [color R G B] [STEP]... [TAIL]
image NAME FILE on MESH X0 Y0 Z0 X1 Y1 Z1 X2 Y2 Z2
unit NAME [STEP]... [TAIL]
end
view iso|front|back|left|right|top|bottom
background R G B
.fi
.RE
.PP
where each
.I STEP
is a
.BI move " DX DY DZ"
or a
.BI turn " x|y|z DEG"
.RB [ about
.IR "X Y Z" ].
The parts of an OBJ file with several objects are named
.IB name / part .
A color (values 0 to 1) replaces that of the file.
The steps of a mesh place it, in order, a turn about the origin unless
it names a point.
A picture (PPM P6, or PAM P7 of RGB or RGB_ALPHA) fills the
parallelogram of its corners X0 (lower left), X1 (lower right) and X2
(upper left), in the frame of the mesh MESH of a line above, and moves
with it.
Pictures are blended over the meshes by their opacity, farthest first;
transparent pixels cannot be picked.
The background is gray unless given.
.PP
The optional
.I TAIL
of a mesh, as
.B place \-s
writes it from an assembly file
.RI ( assembly (5)),
is its insertion path or the mesh it travels with:
.PP
.RS
.nf
path STEP...
with NAME
.fi
.RE
.PP
a turn of a path about the origin of the mesh at its place unless it
names a point.
The order of the mesh lines is the assembly sequence, which
.IR view (1)
plays with + and \-: a mesh goes in along its path from its start, the
start being its place with the steps undone, the last one first; a mesh
with
.B with
moves with the mesh it names, and one with neither stays at its place.
.SS Units
The lines between
.B unit
and its
.B end
are a unit, as
.B place \-s
writes a subassembly: they lie in the frame of the unit at its place,
which its steps give as those of a mesh, and their names are under its
name, so that a mesh
.B cap
in the unit
.B knob
in the unit
.B front
is front/knob/cap, and so are the names after
.B with
and
.BR on .
Units nest.
The tail of a unit moves it as one, after the lines in it.
.SH SEE ALSO
plicad(7), place(1), tomesh(1), view(1), assembly(5)
